{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"description":"Open a URL in the browser and wait for the page to load. Use when: you need a real browser: the page needs JavaScript, redirects, cookies or browser state. Do not use when: For plain static content a normal HTTP fetch is cheaper; use this tool only when JavaScript, browser state or interaction is required. Returns: the final URL and HTTP status. Next: snapshot or read to inspect the page.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"url":{"description":"the URL to open (http or https)","type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"name":"open"},{"description":"Deprecated alias of \"open\"; use \"open\" instead. Open a URL in the browser and wait for the page to load. Use when: you need a real browser: the page needs JavaScript, redirects, cookies or browser state. Do not use when: For plain static content a normal HTTP fetch is cheaper; use this tool only when JavaScript, browser state or interaction is required. Returns: the final URL and HTTP status. Next: snapshot or read to inspect the page.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"url":{"description":"the URL to open (http or https)","type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"name":"goto"},{"description":"Render the accessibility tree of the current page as text. Use when: you need the current interactive state of the page with stable @refs for elements. Do not use when: you only need the page text (use read or a plain fetch); For plain static content a normal HTTP fetch is cheaper; use this tool only when JavaScript, browser state or interaction is required. Returns: the accessibility tree (with --diff: only the changes since the last snapshot). Next: click, fill or get on a @ref.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"compact":{"description":"omit non-interactive structural nodes","type":"boolean"},"depth":{"description":"maximum tree depth; 0 means unlimited","type":"integer"},"interactive":{"description":"include only interactive nodes","type":"boolean"},"selector":{"description":"CSS selector or @ref restricting the snapshot subtree","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"urls":{"description":"include link URLs","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"snapshot"},{"description":"Click the element matching a CSS selector or @ref. Use when: you need to activate an element (button, link, menu item). Do not use when: you only need to read state (use get or snapshot). Returns: the click result. Next: snapshot to observe the new page state.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"selector":{"description":"CSS selector or @ref of the element","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"}},"required":["selector"],"type":"object"},"name":"click"},{"description":"Fill a text input or textarea with a value, replacing its current content. Use when: you need to set a form field to a known value (replaces existing content). Do not use when: the element already has the value or you need to append (use type). Returns: the fill result. Next: press Enter or click the submit button.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"selector":{"description":"CSS selector or @ref of the input","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"value":{"description":"the value to fill","type":"string"}},"required":["selector","value"],"type":"object"},"name":"fill"},{"description":"Type text into the focused or selected element, appending to its current content. Use when: you need to type text that appends to the current field content. Do not use when: you need to replace the content (use fill). Returns: the type result. Next: press Enter or snapshot the field state.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"selector":{"description":"CSS selector or @ref of the input (optional)","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"value":{"description":"the text to type","type":"string"}},"required":["value"],"type":"object"},"name":"type"},{"description":"Press a keyboard key (e.g. Enter, Escape, Tab, ArrowDown). Use when: you need to send a key such as Enter or Escape. Do not use when: you need to type a longer text (use type or fill). Returns: the press result. Next: snapshot to observe the new state.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"key":{"description":"the key to press","type":"string"},"selector":{"description":"CSS selector or @ref of the element to receive the key (optional)","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"}},"required":["key"],"type":"object"},"name":"press"},{"description":"Wait for a browser condition (kind: selector, text, url, ms, load). Use when: the page is still loading or an element is not yet in the expected state. Do not use when: you need a fixed pause (prefer an explicit condition over a sleep). Returns: the wait result. Next: snapshot or read to inspect the settled page.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"kind":{"description":"condition kind: selector, text, url, ms, load","type":"string"},"load":{"description":"load state: load, domcontentloaded, networkidle","type":"string"},"ms":{"description":"duration in milliseconds for kind=ms","type":"integer"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"state":{"description":"selector state: visible, hidden, attached, detached","type":"string"},"value":{"description":"selector, text, or URL substring depending on kind","type":"string"}},"required":["kind"],"type":"object"},"name":"wait"},{"description":"Render the current page (or the page at url) as markdown in the symfetch output schema. Use when: you need the page content as clean markdown with frontmatter (title, url, fetched_at). Do not use when: For plain static content a normal HTTP fetch is cheaper; use this tool only when JavaScript, browser state or interaction is required. Returns: the rendered markdown document. Next: open another URL or find links on the page.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"url":{"description":"URL to open and read (optional; defaults to the current page)","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"read"},{"description":"Inspect the page or an element (kind: text, html, value, attr, title, url, count, box, styles, visible, enabled, checked). Use when: you need one specific value of the page or an element. Do not use when: you need the whole interactive tree (use snapshot). Returns: the inspected value. Next: snapshot or find for further navigation.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"attribute":{"description":"attribute name for kind=attr","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"inspection kind","type":"string"},"selector":{"description":"CSS selector or @ref (not needed for title/url)","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"}},"required":["kind"],"type":"object"},"name":"get"},{"description":"Find elements by semantic query (kind: text, role, label, placeholder, alt, css, xpath, ref; action: goto, focus, click). Use when: you need to locate elements semantically and address them by stable @refs. Do not use when: you already have a working CSS selector or @ref. Returns: the matching elements with their stable @refs. Next: click, fill or get on the returned @ref.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"action":{"description":"action to perform on the match: goto, focus, click","type":"string"},"exact":{"description":"require an exact text match","type":"boolean"},"index":{"description":"match index when several elements match (0-based)","type":"integer"},"kind":{"description":"query kind: text, role, label, placeholder, alt, css, xpath, ref","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"optional accessible name filter","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"the query value","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"value":{"description":"optional value for the action","type":"string"}},"required":["kind","query"],"type":"object"},"name":"find"},{"description":"Fetch a web page with the plain-HTTP fetch pipeline (no browser) and return LLM-optimized content in the SymFetch contract. Use when: you need fast fetch of static content, batch fetch, or Wayback discovery without a browser session. Do not use when: you need JavaScript, browser state or interaction (use open/snapshot/read). Returns: markdown (default), json, or text in the SymFetch output schema. Next: read or open when the page needs a real browser.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"char_limit":{"description":"Per-page character limit for truncate-and-store (default 15000)","type":"integer"},"content_boundaries":{"description":"Wrap fetched content in unforgeable boundaries (default true in MCP mode)","type":"boolean"},"css_selector":{"description":"CSS selector to extract specific elements (e.g. 'table.pricing', '.article-body')","type":"string"},"format":{"description":"Output format: markdown (default), json, text","enum":["markdown","json","text"],"type":"string"},"frontmatter":{"description":"Prepend YAML frontmatter with metadata (title, url, fetched_at, lang, tokens)","type":"boolean"},"include_links":{"description":"Append a Links section with all hrefs (default false)","type":"boolean"},"injection_patterns":{"description":"Path to a custom prompt-injection pattern file","type":"string"},"max_chars":{"description":"Maximum characters in output (default 20000)","type":"integer"},"no_cache":{"description":"Force a fresh fetch instead of using the response cache","type":"boolean"},"no_injection_scan":{"description":"Disable the bounded prompt-injection scan (logged; default false)","type":"boolean"},"query":{"description":"BM25 query for relevance filtering. Returns only sections matching the query, preserving headings and structure.","type":"string"},"raw":{"description":"Return raw decoded response body without semantic processing","type":"boolean"},"schema_path":{"description":"JSON-LD query path. Typed selectors (e.g. '@Recipe:name') filter by @type then traverse a dot-path.","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"store_full_text":{"description":"Enable truncate-and-store for long pages (default false)","type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"description":"Return only the top K relevant sections when query is set (0 = all)","type":"integer"},"url":{"description":"the URL to fetch (http or https)","type":"string"},"wayback_fallback":{"description":"Fall back to the Wayback Machine on 404/thin content","type":"boolean"},"wayback_timestamp":{"description":"Specific Wayback timestamp to fetch (empty = latest)","type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"name":"fetch_url"},{"description":"Fetch multiple URLs concurrently with the plain-HTTP fetch pipeline and return results in input order. Use when: you need several pages at once and each is independent. Do not use when: you need one page (use fetch_url) or browser interaction. Returns: a per-URL array in input order; one failure does not abort the batch. Next: read or open when a result needs a real browser.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"char_limit":{"description":"Per-page character limit for truncate-and-store (default 15000)","type":"integer"},"concurrency":{"description":"Maximum parallel fetches (default 4, max 8)","type":"integer"},"content_boundaries":{"description":"Wrap fetched content in unforgeable boundaries (default true in MCP mode)","type":"boolean"},"format":{"description":"Output format for each result: markdown, json, text","type":"string"},"frontmatter":{"description":"Prepend YAML frontmatter to each result","type":"boolean"},"include_links":{"description":"Append a Links section to each result","type":"boolean"},"injection_patterns":{"description":"Path to a custom prompt-injection pattern file","type":"string"},"max_chars":{"description":"Per-page character budget (default 20000)","type":"integer"},"no_cache":{"description":"Force fresh fetches instead of using the response cache","type":"boolean"},"no_injection_scan":{"description":"Disable the bounded prompt-injection scan (logged; default false)","type":"boolean"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"store_full_text":{"description":"Enable truncate-and-store for each page (default false)","type":"boolean"},"urls":{"description":"URLs to fetch (max 20)","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["urls"],"type":"object"},"name":"fetch_batch"},{"description":"Retrieve full content stored behind a truncated output. Use when: a fetch or other output returned a cache handle. Do not use when: you do not have a cache_id. Returns: the full cached content or the requested line range. Next: use the returned content as the complete source.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"cache_id":{"description":"unified output cache id, for example out_0123456789ab","type":"string"},"range":{"description":"optional 1-indexed inclusive line range a-b","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"}},"required":["cache_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"cache_get"},{"description":"List available Wayback Machine snapshots for a URL. Returns timestamps, HTTP status codes, and MIME types for each captured version. Use when: you need to know whether and when a page was archived, or find a historical version. Do not use when: you need the current live page (use fetch_url). Returns: an array of snapshots with timestamp, url, status, mime_type, digest. Next: fetch the archived URL directly if a snapshot fits.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"from":{"description":"Start date filter (format: YYYYMMDD or YYYYMMDDHHmmss)","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of snapshots to return (default 100)","type":"integer"},"match_type":{"description":"URL matching mode: exact (default), prefix, or host","enum":["exact","prefix","host"],"type":"string"},"session":{"description":"session name (default: default)","type":"string"},"to":{"description":"End date filter (format: YYYYMMDD or YYYYMMDDHHmmss)","type":"string"},"url":{"description":"The URL to look up in the Wayback Machine","type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"name":"wayback_snapshots"}]}}
